{"at":"2026-10-29T06:28:56.747Z","component":"Historical plural selection module","evidence":["101dc75b3918c29a21469faf06309a53bcc5b7242688ff2729ebe034e4a2e9c1","304218093e60be1bf56d8c2b90a3360488487cd00c90012dae051416d81c9d20","41cd9e12b34b41a97e85897dece77ea13596dc6e1333666a54ed0164ccbfcf2b","42d3d7b1bb9fbea363ce1e88d1bbf29b8dfcf686e5b33047ef2b627e319e4650","4b722c9c7f7e4d566f198e39de290440cd9c10dfbdf435fba0037c9a2b87306b","8b49643b75b1cbfc156af08b2138c058e46df78865817563b87875386c6c8569","a5f9d60689365dc2d425f953ec2d535bbcff509f68c278a8d185a4966dcdeb40","cc9e24b656425aa93c909c6572db27405f878208033832be4c1269e111d7dd07","cd410daf32f13652bcb0d9d90f5f04b213c4991b4791af3dbbf0b4bf1b874642","dea2d22173df08d5f63c4312d0fb60c40c96d76ea6e6764d075c0413a7723639"],"id":"7a116bc419de80d537589d7141e4f47e87ce8a8415b2f45ed7d1956acea023f4","kind":"lesson","paths":["mail/modules/PluralForm.sys.mjs","mail/base/test/unit/test_pluralForm-english.js","mail/base/test/unit/test_pluralForm-irish.js","mail/base/test/unit/xpcshell.toml","mail/base/content/mailWindowOverlay.js"],"quotes":[{"id":"42d3d7b1bb9fbea363ce1e88d1bbf29b8dfcf686e5b33047ef2b627e319e4650","text":"    const [numForms, pluralFunc] = this.getPluralRule();\n    this.numForms = () => numForms;"},{"id":"a5f9d60689365dc2d425f953ec2d535bbcff509f68c278a8d185a4966dcdeb40","text":"      case \"is\":\n      case \"mk\":\n        return [\n          4,"},{"id":"4b722c9c7f7e4d566f198e39de290440cd9c10dfbdf435fba0037c9a2b87306b","text":"    document.l10n.setAttributes(menuItem, \"menu-file-get-next-n-news-msgs\", {\n      count: folder.server.maxArticles,\n    });"}],"repository":"thunderbird","source":{"basis":"Quoted evidence supports the claim; its interpretation still needs current-source checks.","revision":"fb489227ae6e973b0bf16fff88cdfd27a42c55bd","sourceAt":"2025-10-31T10:40:43+13:00","type":"extraction"},"status":"supported","supersedes":[],"text":"The owned replacement lazily installs get(number, semicolonString) and numForms() functions for the primary locale language. It removes makeGetter/ruleNum and the broad legacy-rule matrix. The retained English/Irish tests cover those common calls and fallback behavior, not every changed locale branch. In particular, is/mk move from two to four forms and mt reaches the two-form default; these source deltas are not a linguistic correctness claim. The checked later news-menu caller uses Fluent, so the historical helper is not a current API recommendation.","title":"The PluralForm copy preserves common calls while changing legacy helpers, locale rules and test coverage","version":1,"visibility":"shared"}
